\begin{equation*} b_{g} = \frac{\sum _d n_{g,d}}{\sum _d \sum _g n_{g,d}}, \end{equation*}\end{document}where ng, d is the number of counts for gene g in droplet d and the sum over d is taken over all droplets with <Nemp UMIs (Fig. 1). The species-mixing experiment allows us to compare how accurately bg recapitulates the true background expression found within each cell, revealing that any value of Nemp < 100 produces a good correlation, with the best correlation given when Nemp < 10 (Supplementary Fig. S2).

